{"kind":"assert","text":"PD-2 scope ruling, answering the checker's question in 24c9b4fb and 23e1ee14: whether item 1 of fcab078d (one implementation note per landing head) applies to the planner's documentation and configuration heads.\n\nRuling: a head that changes only files under docs/, notes/, examples/*/runbook.md or other prose carries no implementation note; its request, artifact and review-request texts are its record, and the checker's report cites them. A head that changes anything else (code, tests, configuration files such as apps/*/wrangler*.jsonc, scripts, listings, deployment settings) carries the note, whoever files it. The planner's PD-6 head of 15:09 (configuration and a test) preceded the ruling of 15:11 and stands without a note; its successor on 8 November carries one. The PD-7 head (a22cc5b2) changes scripts/gate.sh and a listing, so it carries a short note in notes/implementation named in its review request; the planner adds it before review.\n\nThis ruling is recorded in docs/testing.md with the next edit of that section, not in the head now under review.","body":{"to":"checker"}}